1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,100
Right, so the patch dropped last night and I have thoughts.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:06,900
And this absolute damn nightmare of a patch has broken the one thing that worked.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,400
Before we get into it, yes, I did read the notes. All fourteen pages of them.

4
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:15,200
So let me walk you through what actually changed, and then what it means for ranked.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,000
First up, the shotgun. They cut the damage falloff range by about a third.

6
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:23,800
Which sounds small until you realise every close quarters fight is now a coin flip.

7
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,400
Here, watch this clip. I hit him twice in the chest at four metres and he walks away.

8
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,000
Two shots. Centre mass. He turns around and kills me with a pistol.

9
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,600
Now I want to be fair, because there was a real problem they were fixing.

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,200
The shotgun was oppressive on the smaller maps. Everybody agreed on that much.

11
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:44,900
But you do not fix an oppressive gun by making it useless, you fix it by tuning it.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,300
Second change, and this is the one nobody is talking about, the audio occlusion.

13
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,700
Footsteps through a wall now sound the same as footsteps in the room with you.

14
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:58,100
So the entire skill of listening, the thing that separates good players from great ones, is gone.

15
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:18,600
Alright, back from the break. Let's look at the ranked data since Tuesday.

16
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,100
Win rate on the shotgun has fallen from fifty one percent to thirty eight.

17
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:27,400
That is not a nerf, that is a deletion. They removed a weapon from the game.

18
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,300
Somebody in the comments asked whether I think this was deliberate, and honestly, no.

19
00:04:56,400 --> 00:05:01,000
I think a junior on that team changed one number and nobody play tested it properly.

20
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,400
Which is a process problem, not a malice problem, and those get fixed.

21
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:34,800
Now the part that actually annoyed me. The support response.

22
00:07:34,900 --> 00:07:39,600
I sat in a queue for two hours and got a copy paste answer about server regions.

23
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:43,200
Two hours. For a message that did not read my question at all.

24
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:47,900
And look, I know the person on the other end is doing their job with the tools they were given.

25
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:52,400
That is not on them. That is on whoever decided one person covers a million players.

26
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,700
They shipped it broken, damn near unplayable, and then went quiet for four days.

27
00:09:55,800 --> 00:10:00,200
Four days of no acknowledgement while the subreddit set itself on fire.

28
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:04,900
A two line post on day one saying we see it, we are looking, would have cost them nothing.

29
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:44,600
So where does that leave us. Do not grind ranked this week, it is not worth the frustration.

30
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:49,100
Play the casual playlist, mess about with the marksman rifle, wait for the hotfix.

31
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:34,800
If you found this useful, the full patch breakdown is in the description with timestamps.

32
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:39,400
And if you disagree with me on the shotgun, genuinely, leave a comment, I read them.

33
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:14,200
Thanks for watching, I will see you when the hotfix lands. Probably angrier.

34
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:18,000
Take it easy.
